18505348,2026-01-06,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"I am filing this complaint regarding improper handling of an unauthorized transaction dispute on my Apple Card involving a lost physical card and inconsistent fraud determinations by Goldman Sachs Bank USA. 

Timeline and Facts On XX/XX/XXXX, two unauthorized transactions appeared on my Apple Card : XXXX XXXX for {$3200.00} XXXX XXXX XXXX for {$20.00} At the time these transactions occurred, I was at home asleep and did not authorize either charge. 
I immediately contacted Goldman Sachs Apple Card support upon seeing the charges. I was informed that the physical card was used for both transactions. 
I then discovered that my physical Apple Card was missing, indicating it had been lost or stolen. 
I immediately reported both transactions as fraudulent and unauthorized, my card was frozen, and a replacement card was issued. 

Inconsistent Dispute Handling On XX/XX/XXXX, the {$20.00} XXXX transaction was credited and ruled unauthorized, confirming fraud had occurred. 
However, no decision was provided at that time for the {$3200.00} Micro Center transaction, even though : Both charges occurred on the same date Both charges used the same lost physical card Both charges were disputed at the same time for the same reason On XX/XX/XXXX, Goldman Sachs issued a dispute result stating that the {$3200.00} Micro Center charge was authorized and would remain on my account. 

This determination is illogical and inconsistent. A single lost card fraud event can not result in one transaction being unauthorized while another, larger transaction from the same incident is deemed authorized. 

Reopened Disputes and Continued Errors I immediately contacted Apple Card support on XX/XX/XXXX to reopen the dispute and explained the inconsistency. 
XXXX agreed the situation did not make sense and reopened the dispute. 
On XX/XX/XXXX, I was again notified that the XXXX XXXX transaction was ruled authorized and the charge would remain. 
I immediately contacted support again, explained the same facts, and the dispute was reopened once more. 

This cycle of reopening and re-denial without addressing the core issue has caused significant concern and demonstrates a failure to conduct a proper fraud investigation. 

Key Issues Not Addressed by the Bank Goldman Sachs has not explained : How a lost/stolen physical card fraud event can result in one unauthorized transaction being credited and another being deemed authorized What evidence supports the claim that the {$3200.00} transaction was authorized Why the smaller XXXX transaction was credited as fraud almost immediately, while the larger Micro Center transaction was denied Why the same dispute continues to be reopened without a meaningful or corrected investigation Why the banks determinations contradict their own fraud acknowledgment",,GOLDMAN SACHS BANK USA,CA,91202,,Web,2026-01-06,Closed with monetary relief,Yes
