I have filed official identity theft reports, and documentation supporting my claim is enclosed. Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) 605B, upon receipt of an identity theft report, a furnisher of information is required to block the reporting of fraudulent information within four ( 4 ) business days and must cease all collection and reporting activity related to the fraudulent account. 

Additionally, if XXXX XXXX XXXX  sold or transferred this account, it is improper for multiple entities to report active balances simultaneously. Reporting inconsistent balances for the same alleged debt constitutes inaccurate and misleading reporting under the FCRA.

Accordingly, I am demanding the following : 1. Immediate deletion of this account from all consumer credit reporting agencies 2. Cessation of all collection activity related to this account 3. Written confirmation that the account has been permanently removed and is no longer being pursued This letter is not a request to correct, validate, or update the balance. Any attempt to do so would be inappropriate, as the account itself is the result of identity theft and must be removed in its entirety. 

If this account is not promptly blocked and deleted as required by law, I will pursue all available remedies, including complaints with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) and enforcement of my rights under the FCRA. 

Please confirm in writing once deletion has been completed. 

