18539495,2026-01-07,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Fees or interest,Problem with fees,"XX/XX/year>, I received an email stating that a $ XXXX fee would be charged to my card. I have never had this kind of fee so when I reached out to the company through their chat support in the mobile app, also on XX/XX/XXXX, I was told it was so the company could continue to provide the "" special benefits '' associated with my card such as 2 % unlimited cash back, fraud protection, and XXXX liability. I have this on other cards and do not pay a fee. I have had this on my card since I got it and have not had to pay a fee to have these benefits. And these benefits are not above and beyond other cards. They are pretty standard. When I inquired with the company about who is being charged this fee, the response from the customer service rep was that a subset of the 2 % cash back cardholders were going to be charged this fee. I asked for the criteria that determined those selected, and his response was the company did not provide that information. The only info he provided was that not everyone with the same card as me will have to pay the fee, only those receiving the notification via email or mail. When I asked about the "" opt out '' option for the fee, he said that mean I would have to cancel my card and close my account. My response was that's not an opt out, then, it's either pay the fee or close your account. Closing the account is VERY different than opting out of a fee for benefits that are provided by nearly every type of credit card. I do not want to pay a {$120.00} annual fee for something that is a minor benefit, and I do not want to close my account because that produces a negative hit on my credit report, which I'm already trying to repair. So it's a "" damned if you do, and damned if you don't '' scenario, which does not seem like a fair practice when they already charge exorbitant interest on the balances.",,"SOFI TECHNOLOGIES, INC.",IL,61571,,Web,2026-01-07,Closed with explanation,Yes
