Additionally, the merchant name on my statement ( XXXX ) does not clearly correspond to the storefront ( XXXX ), which is a known indicator of merchant-of-record fraud and should have prompted heightened review rather than acceptance of unsupported merchant claims. 

Under the Fair Credit Billing Act and Regulation XXXX, a charge is disputable when goods are not received as agreed. A merchants claim of shipment without verifiable proof of delivery does not satisfy this requirement. 

