Despite this explicit denial of authorization, PennyMac subsequently : Initiated a loan application, Distributed loan-related disclosures, Sent repeated follow-up communications over the last ten days, and Pulled my credit without my authorization. 

This conduct is unacceptable and potentially violative of federal consumer protection laws, including but not limited to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and RESPA servicing and solicitation standards, as well as general prohibitions against unauthorized credit activity. 

Let me be clear : I did not authorize a loan application. 
I did not consent to any credit inquiry. 
I did not approve the issuance of disclosures or loan documentation. 

I hereby demand the following actions be taken immediately : 1. Written confirmation that all loan applications, disclosures, and related files have been permanently closed and withdrawn. 
2. Written confirmation that no further credit inquiries will be made, and that any credit inquiry already performed has been corrected, withdrawn, or addressed in accordance with applicable law. 
3. Identification of the individual ( s ) involved in initiating unauthorized activity. 
4. Assurance that my information will not be used for any further marketing, solicitation, or loan activity without my express written consent. 

Failure to resolve this matter promptly and in writing will leave me no choice but to escalate this issue through formal regulatory channels, including the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) and other appropriate oversight bodies. 

I expect written confirmation of resolution within XXXX business days of receipt of this notice. 
Regards, XXXX XXXX XXXX",,"PENNYMAC LOAN SERVICES, LLC.",NV,890XX,,Web,2026-01-13,Closed with explanation,Yes
